fetched from the GitHub releases API, so the site build is deterministic
and builds with no network.

React Bits (hero prism backdrop)
--------------------------------
`site/components/landing/prism-backdrop.tsx` adapts the `Prism` WebGL
background — the ray-marched prism SDF, its grade, and the ogl mount — from
React Bits, by way of the okengine documentation site:

  https://github.com/DavidHDev/react-bits

Upstream path:
  src/content/Backgrounds/Prism/Prism.tsx

Licence: MIT License (LICENSE in that repository)
Copyright (c) 2025 David Haz

Adapted, not copied verbatim: the prop surface is replaced by fixed tuning,
the `lightMode` flag follows the live `dark` class, the render loop
re-measures its percentage-sized host, device pixel ratio is capped, `ogl`
loads after mount, and the loop obeys `prefers-reduced-motion` by painting one
frame with time frozen.

